IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-nouns`
IMPORT `g6-notice-and-hearing`
IMPORT `g6-payment`

-- g6-tests-payment.l4: tests of ss.48-51.
-- Expected values were decided from the Hebrew of ss.48-51 (law.wiki lines 378-391; gazette p. 195) and from
-- Interpretation Law s.10 before any run.  The dates:
--   a payment demand delivered Wednesday 2 June 2027: 30 days from it, IL s.10(a), end on Friday 2 July 2027
--     (3 to 30 June are 28 days, 1 July the 29th, 2 July the 30th); if Friday 2 and Saturday 3 July are days
--     of rest (IL s.10(c), kind D) the last day is Sunday 4 July 2027, 32 days after delivery.
--   trap T16, a violator who made no representations: the notice of intention delivered Wednesday 3 March 2027;
--     s.43's 30 days end on Friday 2 April 2027; the notice is treated as a demand delivered that day (s.44(d));
--     s.48's 30 days from it end on Sunday 2 May 2027: 60 days after the notice, as the trap says.
--     With Friday 2 and Saturday 3 April as days of rest the s.43 period ends Sunday 4 April, and s.48's 30 days
--     end on Tuesday 4 May 2027 (62 days after the notice).

§ `Tests of ss 48 to 51`

§§ `Fixtures`

`no day of rest at all` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS EMPTY
`Friday 2 and Saturday 3 July 2027 as days of rest`  MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST (YMD 2027 7 2), (YMD 2027 7 3)
`Friday 2 and Saturday 3 April 2027 as days of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST (YMD 2027 4 2), (YMD 2027 4 3)

`the day the payment demand is delivered` MEANS YMD 2027 6 2

-- Positional fields of `Notice of intention`: delivered on, in writing, states act+date, states amount, period (days),
-- right (s 43), deemed demand, power to add, intention to publish name.
`a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` MEANS `Notice of intention` OF YMD 2027 3 3, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, JUST 30, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE

§§ `s 48: 30 days from the delivery of the demand, IL s.10(a), and IL s.10(c) applied (kind D)`

#ASSERT `s 48 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the payment demand` `the day the payment demand is delivered` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 7 2
#ASSERT `s 48 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the payment demand` `the day the payment demand is delivered` `Friday 2 and Saturday 3 July 2027 as days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2027 7 4
#ASSERT `s 48 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the payment demand, without s 10(c)` `the day the payment demand is delivered` EQUALS YMD 2027 7 2
#ASSERT `s 48 — the number of days from the delivery of the demand to the last day for payment` `the day the payment demand is delivered` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `s 48 — the number of days from the delivery of the demand to the last day for payment` `the day the payment demand is delivered` `Friday 2 and Saturday 3 July 2027 as days of rest` EQUALS 32

-- Both edges of the payment period (fork F-ACTDAY).  A payment made ON the day the demand is delivered is "within 30
-- days" of it; a day before is not; the last day is inside.
#ASSERT NOT `s 48 — the day` (YMD 2027 6 1) `is within the period for payment that runs from` `the day the payment demand is delivered` `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT     `s 48 — the day` (YMD 2027 6 2) `is within the period for payment that runs from` `the day the payment demand is delivered` `with` `no day of rest at all`
-- The strict reading, callable: the period starts the day AFTER delivery.
#ASSERT NOT `s 48 — counting the day after delivery as the first day, the day` (YMD 2027 6 2) `is within the period for payment that runs from` `the day the payment demand is delivered` `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT     `s 48 — counting the day after delivery as the first day, the day` (YMD 2027 6 3) `is within the period for payment that runs from` `the day the payment demand is delivered` `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT     `s 48 — counting the day after delivery as the first day, the day` (YMD 2027 7 2) `is within the period for payment that runs from` `the day the payment demand is delivered` `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT NOT `s 48 — counting the day after delivery as the first day, the day` (YMD 2027 7 3) `is within the period for payment that runs from` `the day the payment demand is delivered` `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT     `s 48 — the day` (YMD 2027 6 3) `is within the period for payment that runs from` `the day the payment demand is delivered` `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT     `s 48 — the day` (YMD 2027 7 2) `is within the period for payment that runs from` `the day the payment demand is delivered` `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT NOT `s 48 — the day` (YMD 2027 7 3) `is within the period for payment that runs from` `the day the payment demand is delivered` `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT     `s 48 — the day` (YMD 2027 7 4) `is within the period for payment that runs from` `the day the payment demand is delivered` `with` `Friday 2 and Saturday 3 July 2027 as days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `s 48 — the day` (YMD 2027 7 5) `is within the period for payment that runs from` `the day the payment demand is delivered` `with` `Friday 2 and Saturday 3 July 2027 as days of rest`

-- Trap T16: a violator who made no representations.  The notice treated as a demand is delivered at the end of the
-- s.43 period, and s.48's 30 days run from it: 60 days after the notice.
#ASSERT `s 48 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the payment demand` (`s 44(d) — the day the notice of intention is treated as a payment demand delivered` `a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` NOTHING `no day of rest at all`) `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 5 2
#ASSERT (Day (YMD 2027 5 2)) MINUS (Day (YMD 2027 3 3)) EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `s 48 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the payment demand` (`s 44(d) — the day the notice of intention is treated as a payment demand delivered` `a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` NOTHING `Friday 2 and Saturday 3 April 2027 as days of rest`) `Friday 2 and Saturday 3 April 2027 as days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2027 5 4
#ASSERT (Day (YMD 2027 5 4)) MINUS (Day (YMD 2027 3 3)) EQUALS 62

-- The period the demand states (F-PERIOD): none stated, the same as s.48; 45 stated, the alternative takes it.
#ASSERT `s 48 — the last day for payment, when a period stated in the demand governs` `the day the payment demand is delivered` NOTHING `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 7 2
#ASSERT `s 48 — the last day for payment, when a period stated in the demand governs` `the day the payment demand is delivered` (JUST 30) `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 7 2
#ASSERT `s 48 — the last day for payment, when a period stated in the demand governs` `the day the payment demand is delivered` (JUST 45) `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 7 17
#ASSERT `s 48 — the last day for payment, when a period stated in the demand governs` `the day the payment demand is delivered` (JUST 15) `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 6 17

§§ `s 49: late payment, the days of delay, and the amount owed (a named refusal without the Interest and Linkage Law's figures)`

-- Late is after the last day; a payment on the last day is on time.
#ASSERT NOT `s 49 — the payment of` (YMD 2027 7 2) `is late, the last day for payment being` (YMD 2027 7 2)
#ASSERT     `s 49 — the payment of` (YMD 2027 7 3) `is late, the last day for payment being` (YMD 2027 7 2)
#ASSERT NOT `s 49 — the payment of` (YMD 2027 6 20) `is late, the last day for payment being` (YMD 2027 7 2)
-- The days of delay: from the day after the last day to the day of payment.
#ASSERT `s 49 — the days of delay, from the day after` (YMD 2027 7 2) `until` (YMD 2027 7 12) EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `s 49 — the days of delay, from the day after` (YMD 2027 7 2) `until` (YMD 2027 7 3) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 49 — the days of delay, from the day after` (YMD 2027 7 2) `until` (YMD 2027 7 2) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 49 — the days of delay, from the day after` (YMD 2027 7 2) `until` (YMD 2027 6 20) EQUALS 0

-- A payment on time owes neither interest nor fees, whatever the caller supplied.
#ASSERT `s 49 — the amount owed on a sanction of` 20_000 `when the payment is late:` FALSE `with shekel interest` NOTHING `and arrears fees` NOTHING EQUALS 20_000
#ASSERT `s 49 — the amount owed on a sanction of` 20_000 `when the payment is late:` FALSE `with shekel interest` (JUST 150) `and arrears fees` (JUST 50) EQUALS 20_000
-- A late payment owes the shekel interest and the arrears fees as the caller computes them: 20,000 + 150 + 50.
#ASSERT `s 49 — the amount owed on a sanction of` 20_000 `when the payment is late:` TRUE `with shekel interest` (JUST 150) `and arrears fees` (JUST 50) EQUALS 20_200
-- A figure the caller does not supply is a named refusal, never zero.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 49 — the amount owed on a sanction of` 20_000 `when the payment is late:` TRUE `with shekel interest` NOTHING `and arrears fees` (JUST 50) BECAUSE "s 49 — the shekel interest and the arrears fees are fixed by the Interest and Linkage Law, whose rates are not in the sources, and none was supplied"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 49 — the amount owed on a sanction of` 20_000 `when the payment is late:` TRUE `with shekel interest` (JUST 150) `and arrears fees` NOTHING BECAUSE "s 49 — the shekel interest and the arrears fees are fixed by the Interest and Linkage Law, whose rates are not in the sources, and none was supplied"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 49 — the amount owed on a sanction of` 20_000 `when the payment is late:` TRUE `with shekel interest` NOTHING `and arrears fees` NOTHING
-- The alternative (F-INTEREST): rates for the whole delay, simple, on the sanction alone: 20,000 x (1 + 0.01 + 0.005).
#ASSERT `s 49 — the amount owed, at simple rates, on a sanction of` 20_000 `when the payment is late:` TRUE `with a shekel interest rate for the whole delay of` (JUST 0.01) `and an arrears fees rate of` (JUST 0.005) EQUALS 20_300
#ASSERT `s 49 — the amount owed, at simple rates, on a sanction of` 20_000 `when the payment is late:` FALSE `with a shekel interest rate for the whole delay of` (JUST 0.01) `and an arrears fees rate of` (JUST 0.005) EQUALS 20_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 49 — the amount owed, at simple rates, on a sanction of` 20_000 `when the payment is late:` TRUE `with a shekel interest rate for the whole delay of` NOTHING `and an arrears fees rate of` (JUST 0.005)

§§ `s 48 and s 49 as one duty: pay in time, or pay with the interest and arrears fees`

-- The demand is delivered on 2 June 2027 (AT 0); the 30 days end on 2 July (AT 30).  The sanction is 20,000.
-- Paid in full on the last day: in time.
#TRACE `s 48 — the violator must pay the financial sanction of` 20_000 `, the demand being delivered on` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `no day of rest at all` `and, if late,` (JUST 150) `and` (JUST 50) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the violator` DOES `pay the financial sanction` `the violator` 20_000 AT 30
-- A part payment is not payment of the sanction: the duty stands.
#TRACE `s 48 — the violator must pay the financial sanction of` 20_000 `, the demand being delivered on` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `no day of rest at all` `and, if late,` (JUST 150) `and` (JUST 50) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the violator` DOES `pay the financial sanction` `the violator` 19_999 AT 30
-- The 30 days pass unpaid: the second rung, pay with interest and arrears fees (20,200), stands without a deadline.
#TRACE `s 48 — the violator must pay the financial sanction of` 20_000 `, the demand being delivered on` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `no day of rest at all` `and, if late,` (JUST 150) `and` (JUST 50) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 31)
-- ... and paying 20,200 late discharges it.
#TRACE `s 48 — the violator must pay the financial sanction of` 20_000 `, the demand being delivered on` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `no day of rest at all` `and, if late,` (JUST 150) `and` (JUST 50) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 31)
    PARTY `the violator` DOES `pay the financial sanction together with the interest and arrears fees` `the violator` 20_200 AT 40
-- ... but 20,000 late does not.
#TRACE `s 48 — the violator must pay the financial sanction of` 20_000 `, the demand being delivered on` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `no day of rest at all` `and, if late,` (JUST 150) `and` (JUST 50) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 31)
    PARTY `the violator` DOES `pay the financial sanction together with the interest and arrears fees` `the violator` 20_000 AT 40
-- With 2 and 3 July as days of rest the 30 days run to day 32: paying on day 32 is in time.
#TRACE `s 48 — the violator must pay the financial sanction of` 20_000 `, the demand being delivered on` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `Friday 2 and Saturday 3 July 2027 as days of rest` `and, if late,` (JUST 150) `and` (JUST 50) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the violator` DOES `pay the financial sanction` `the violator` 20_000 AT 32

§§ `s 50: payment by instalments, at most 12 monthly payments, at the violator's request`

#ASSERT     `s 50(a) — an instalment plan is within what the Law allows` TRUE 12 TRUE
#ASSERT     `s 50(a) — an instalment plan is within what the Law allows` TRUE 1 TRUE
#ASSERT     `s 50(a) — an instalment plan is within what the Law allows` TRUE 6 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 50(a) — an instalment plan is within what the Law allows` TRUE 13 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 50(a) — an instalment plan is within what the Law allows` TRUE 0 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 50(a) — an instalment plan is within what the Law allows` FALSE 12 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 50(a) — an instalment plan is within what the Law allows` TRUE 12 FALSE

-- The Commissioner's power: a MAY, with his own view of the amount and the circumstances.
#TRACE `s 50(a) — the Commissioner may allow payment by instalments` TRUE 12 TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `allow payment of the financial sanction by instalments` `the Commissioner` AT 5
#TRACE `s 50(a) — the Commissioner may allow payment by instalments` TRUE 13 TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 5)
#TRACE `s 50(a) — the Commissioner may allow payment by instalments` TRUE 12 TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 5)

-- (b): a payment missed voids the decision; the balance falls due at once, and s.49 applies.
#ASSERT     `s 50(b) — the decision on instalments is treated as void and the balance falls due at once` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 50(b) — the decision on instalments is treated as void and the balance falls due at once` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 50(b) — the balance of the debt that falls due at once on a sanction of` 12_000 `of which` 3_000 `has been paid` EQUALS 9_000
#ASSERT `s 50(b) — the balance of the debt that falls due at once on a sanction of` 12_000 `of which` 0 `has been paid` EQUALS 12_000
#ASSERT `s 50(b) — the balance of the debt that falls due at once on a sanction of` 12_000 `of which` 12_000 `has been paid` EQUALS 0

§§ `s 51: the sanction is collected for the State Treasury (inert)`

#ASSERT `s 51 — the payee of a financial sanction` EQUALS "the State Treasury"
